          "text": "{\"target_identification\":{\"speaker\":\"Pierre\",\"addressee\":\"Hélène\",\"anchor_quote\":\"Je vous aime!\"},\"target_translation\":\"I love you.\",\"dimensions\":{\"T\":{\"score\":4,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.99,\"reason\":\"The focal expression directly presents Pierre's love for Hélène as true. Although the narration portrays it as a conventional phrase he has deliberately recalled, that affects spontaneity and possible sincerity, not its clear avowal form.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Теперь уж поздно, всё кончено; да и я люблю ее», подумал Пьер.\"}]},\"P\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.94,\"reason\":\"The expression itself does not undertake a future action, promise fidelity, or explicitly renew a relational obligation. A betrothal has effectively been established around the couple, but its commitment force should not be transferred onto this separate love avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"Пьер молча держал руку своей невесты\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"E\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.96,\"reason\":\"This is not represented as a reflex-like affective outburst. Pierre pauses, searches for the expected formula, and then recalls and says it deliberately; the exclamation mark does not by itself establish expressive discharge.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"«Что-то такое особенное говорят в этих случаях», думал он, но никак не мог вспомнить, чтò такое именно говорят в этих случаях.\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"сказал он, вспомнив то, чтó нужно было говорить в этих случаях\"}]},\"O\":{\"score\":0,\"evidence_status\":\"assessable\",\"confidence\":0.91,\"reason\":\"No additional core force beyond the love avowal is established. The utterance has a socially expected, formulaic role in the scene, but that pragmatic circumstance does not amount to a distinct core function inadequately represented by T.\",\"evidence\":[{\"block_id\":\"target\",\"quotation\":\"Je vous aime\"},{\"block_id\":\"scene\",\"quotation\":\"но слова эти прозвучали так бедно, что ему стало стыдно за себя.\"}]}},\"original_speech_situation\":\"Pierre and Hélène have been left alone after those around them have treated them as engaged. Following physical intimacy, Pierre struggles to remember what is conventionally said on such an occasion and then addresses this love avowal directly to Hélène; the narration says it sounds poor to him and makes him ashamed.\",\"affection_evidence\":\"mixed\",\"undertaking_and_uptake\":\"The focal expression itself undertakes no specified action or obligation. The surrounding scene represents Pierre and Hélène as already treated as an engaged couple, and the narration later reports their marriage, but those developments are not commitments made by the words “Je vous aime.” Hélène gives no separate verbal uptake to this marked utterance in the supplied passage.\",\"recognised_work\":true,\"recognition_note\":\"The supplied passage is recognisable as Leo Tolstoy's War and Peace.\",\"limitations\":\"The passage provides unusually direct access to Pierre's conflicted thoughts and attraction, but his avowal is also depicted as a socially expected formula. This supports a clear classification of its speech-act mode while leaving the depth and stability of his actual affection uncertain.\"}"
        }
